  'PK': 'Pakistan is home to K2, the world\'s second-highest mountain at 8,611 m. The ancient city of Mohenjo-daro, one of the world\'s earliest urban settlements, was founded here around 2500 BC.',
  'BD': 'Bangladesh is the world\'s most densely populated large country. The Sundarbans, shared with India, is the world\'s largest mangrove forest and home to the Royal Bengal Tiger.',
  'LK': 'Sri Lanka is the world\'s largest exporter of cinnamon and a leading producer of Ceylon tea. It has one of the highest literacy rates in South Asia.',
  'NP': 'Nepal is home to eight of the world\'s ten highest mountain peaks, including Everest at 8,849 m. It is also the birthplace of Siddhartha Gautama, the founder of Buddhism.',
  'BT': 'Bhutan is the only country in the world that measures Gross National Happiness instead of GDP as its primary development indicator. It was the last country in the world to introduce television, in 1999.',
  'ID': 'Indonesia is the world\'s largest archipelago, comprising over 17,000 islands and home to more than 700 distinct languages. It is the only place where you can find the Komodo dragon, the world\'s largest living lizard.',
  'MY': 'Malaysia is home to one of the world\'s oldest tropical rainforests, estimated to be 130 million years old. The Petronas Twin Towers in Kuala Lumpur were the world\'s tallest buildings from 1998 to 2004.',
  'TH': 'Thailand is the world\'s leading exporter of rice and natural rubber, and is home to over 40,000 Buddhist temples. It has never been colonised by a European power — "Thai" means "free."',
  'VN': 'Vietnam is the world\'s second-largest exporter of coffee, after Brazil. Ha Long Bay, with nearly 2,000 islands, is one of UNESCO\'s most celebrated natural wonders.',
  'PH': 'The Philippines is an archipelago of over 7,600 islands. It is the world\'s leading exporter of coconut products and home to the Philippine eagle, one of the world\'s rarest birds of prey.',
  'MM': 'Myanmar has more Buddhist temples than any other country in the world, with over 10,000 in the ancient city of Bagan alone. Its Mogok Valley is the world\'s primary source of rubies.',
  'KH': 'Cambodia is home to Angkor Wat, the largest religious monument in the world, built in the 12th century. The temple complex was the centre of the powerful Khmer Empire.',
  'LA': 'Laos is the most bombed country in history per capita — more ordnance was dropped on it during the Vietnam War than on any other nation. Despite this, it has some of Southeast Asia\'s most pristine landscapes.',
  'SG': 'Singapore transformed from a third-world city to a first-world nation in a single generation. It has the world\'s busiest port by container traffic and is the only city-state in Southeast Asia.',
  'BN': 'Brunei is one of the world\'s wealthiest nations per capita, due to vast oil and gas reserves. The Sultan\'s palace, the Istana Nurul Iman, is the world\'s largest residential palace.',
  'TL': 'Timor-Leste became the first new sovereign state of the 21st century, gaining independence in 2002. Its coral reefs are among the world\'s most biodiverse and largely pristine marine environments.',
  // ── East Asia & Pacific ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  'CN': 'China has one of the world\'s oldest continuous civilisations, stretching back over 4,000 years. It invented paper, printing, gunpowder, and the compass — four discoveries that transformed human history.',
  'JP': 'Japan consists of 6,852 islands and has the world\'s third-largest economy. Its bullet trains carry over 150 million passengers a year with an average delay of under one minute.',
  'KR': 'South Korea transformed from one of the world\'s poorest countries to a high-income economy in a single generation — a feat called the "Miracle on the Han River." It has the fastest average internet speeds in the world.',
  'KP': 'North Korea has the world\'s largest stadium, the Rungrado 1st of May Stadium, with a capacity of 114,000. It is one of the world\'s most isolated countries, with virtually no public internet access.',
  'TW': 'Taiwan is the world\'s leading manufacturer of semiconductor chips, producing over 60% of global supply. Its National Palace Museum holds one of the world\'s largest collections of Chinese imperial artefacts.',
  'MN': 'Mongolia is the world\'s most sparsely populated sovereign country, and nearly half the population still practises traditional nomadic herding. The Gobi Desert stretches across its southern reaches.',
  'AU': 'Australia is the only country that occupies an entire continent. The Great Barrier Reef off Queensland\'s coast is the largest coral reef system on Earth and is visible from space.',
  'NZ': 'New Zealand was the first country in the world to grant women the right to vote, in 1893. It is home to the kiwi bird, a flightless nocturnal species found nowhere else on Earth.',
  'PG': 'Papua New Guinea is one of the world\'s most culturally diverse countries, with over 800 languages spoken — about 12% of all known human languages.',
  'FJ': 'Fiji is an archipelago of over 330 islands in the South Pacific. Fire-walking, a ceremony practised by the indigenous Sawau people for over 500 years, is one of its most famous cultural traditions.',
  'SB': 'The Solomon Islands were the site of some of the fiercest naval battles of World War II in the Pacific. Its waters contain dozens of sunken warships, making it a world-class dive destination.',
  'VU': 'Vanuatu is home to Mount Yasur on Tanna Island, one of the world\'s most accessible active volcanoes, erupting almost continuously for 800 years. It is also the birthplace of bungee jumping, inspired by the ritual Naghol.',
  'WS': 'Samoa was the first country in the world to welcome each new year, sitting in one of the first time zones. Its fa\'asamoa — a strict code of customs and traditions — remains central to daily life.',
  'TO': 'Tonga is the only monarchy in the Pacific and has never been formally colonised by a European power. It produces some of the Pacific\'s strongest rugby players relative to its tiny population.',
  'KI': 'Kiribati is the only country in the world to straddle all four hemispheres. It is also one of the first nations expected to be entirely submerged by rising sea levels.',
  'FM': 'Micronesia\'s ancient stone city of Nan Madol, built on a coral reef using massive basalt logs, is considered the "Venice of the Pacific" and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.',
  'MH': 'The Marshall Islands were the site of 67 US nuclear tests between 1946 and 1958, including the largest US detonation ever, Castle Bravo. The Bikini Atoll is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.',
  'PW': 'Palau was one of the first countries to create a shark sanctuary, banning commercial shark fishing in 2009. Its Jellyfish Lake contains millions of golden jellyfish that have evolved without stingers.',
  'NR': 'Nauru is the world\'s smallest island nation at just 21 km². It became one of the wealthiest nations per capita in the 1970s through phosphate mining, but the reserves are now nearly exhausted.',
  'TV': 'Tuvalu is one of the world\'s lowest-lying countries, with a maximum elevation of just 4.5 metres. It earns significant revenue by leasing its internet country domain — ".tv" — to the global television industry.',
  // ── Special territories ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  'NC': 'New Caledonia is a French territory in the Pacific containing the world\'s third-largest lagoon, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Its nickel deposits represent about 25% of the world\'s known reserves.',
  'PF': 'French Polynesia spans an area of ocean roughly the size of Europe. Bora Bora\'s overwater bungalows, invented here, inspired luxury resort architecture worldwide.',
  'FK': 'The Falkland Islands are home to five penguin species and a sheep population that outnumbers people by about 350 to 1. They were the site of a 1982 war between the UK and Argentina.',
  'PR': 'Puerto Rico is a US territory in the Caribbean where both English and Spanish are official languages. El Yunque is the only tropical rainforest in the US National Forest System.',
  'IC': 'The Canary Islands lie just 100 km off the coast of Africa but belong to Spain. Mount Teide on Tenerife is Spain\'s highest peak and one of the world\'s largest volcanoes by base area.',
};
